# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which
# rewrites line endings on checkout. Shell scripts must keep LF: a CRLF shell
# script fails on Linux and macOS with errors like
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# scripts/deploy.sh is the guard that stops a deploy from destroying the cost
# budget, so it failing to run on a collaborator's machine would be the worst
# possible thing to leave to chance.
#
# Note: Git Bash on this Windows machine tolerates CRLF, so the failure was NOT
# reproduced locally. This is protection for clones on other platforms.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Normalise text files, and never touch binaries.
* text=auto
*.png binary
